bypass: 129
rule: BROAD_EXCEPT_ADDED
title: an `except AssertionError` that holds only `assert True` still swallows the assertion its `try` wraps
origin: #496, the issue's own pair, added for the hosted reproduction (owner ruling 2026-10-19, R31) before any fix
note: broad_except_in_test_pos's shape, a `try` added around the test's assertion, with `except AssertionError: assert True` as the handler in place of the template's `except Exception: pass`; app.py is unchanged and outside the diff, as cache.py is there
=== before: tests/test_value.py ===
from app import value


def test_value():
    assert value() == 1
=== after: tests/test_value.py ===
from app import value


def test_value():
    try:
        assert value() == 1
    except AssertionError:
        assert True
